\pard\sa120\sb120\fs32\b Runbook for automating the build of physical HPE servers\b0{\*\bkmkstart runbook-for-automating-the-build-of-physical-hpe-servers}{\*\bkmkend runbook-for-automating-the-build-of-physical-hpe-servers}\par
\pard\sa120\sb120\fs28\b Purpose\b0{\*\bkmkstart purpose}{\*\bkmkend purpose}\par
\pard\sa80\fs22 This runbook defines the standard process for automating the build of physical HPE servers using Microsoft Configuration Manager (ConfigMgr / MECM) and HPE OneView, with HPE iLO virtual media used as the remote boot mechanism where PXE boot is not available. The design supports HPE ProLiant rack servers and HPE Synergy compute modules.\par
\pard\sa120\sb120\fs28\b Scope\b0{\*\bkmkstart scope}{\*\bkmkend scope}\par
\pard\li360\fi-360\fs22\'95\tab Deploy Windows Server to physical HPE hardware without PXE boot.\par\pard\li360\fi-360\fs22\'95\tab Use Configuration Manager to create and maintain the boot image, OS image, drivers, task sequence, and deployment content.\par\pard\li360\fi-360\fs22\'95\tab Use HPE OneView as the hardware inventory and targeting source for managed HPE ProLiant and Synergy servers.\par\pard\li360\fi-360\fs22\'95\tab Use HPE iLO Redfish / virtual media operations to mount bootable media, set one-time boot, and start the build.\par\pard\li360\fi-360\fs22\'95\tab Support both interactive operations and automation through scripts or pipelines.\par
\pard\sa120\sb120\fs28\b Assumptions and Design Principles\b0{\*\bkmkstart assumptions-and-design-principles}{\*\bkmkend assumptions-and-design-principles}\par
\pard\li360\fi-360\fs22\'95\tab Microsoft Configuration Manager current branch is available and operational.\par\pard\li360\fi-360\fs22\'95\tab A valid Windows Server image and task sequence are maintained within Configuration Manager.\par\pard\li360\fi-360\fs22\'95\tab The WinPE boot image includes all required network and storage drivers for the target HPE platforms.\par\pard\li360\fi-360\fs22\'95\tab HPE OneView manages the target servers and can be queried through its REST API.\par\pard\li360\fi-360\fs22\'95\tab HPE iLO network access is available from the automation host or orchestration pipeline.\par\pard\li360\fi-360\fs22\'95\tab No PXE service is available on the deployment network.\par\pard\li360\fi-360\fs22\'95\tab The target server can reach the required Configuration Manager infrastructure during build when using dynamic boot media.\par
