rs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx1896\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx10878\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx13958{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 Security / IAM\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 Provide and govern service account permissions and secret storage\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 Prefer secret vault / pipeline secrets; avoid hard-coded credentials.\cell}\row\trowd\trgaph60\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx1896\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx10878\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx13958{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 Change Manager\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 Approve production builds and maintain CRQ traceability where required.\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 Recommended for controlled environments.\cell}\row\pard\sa120\par
\pard\sa120\sb120\fs28\b High-Level Architecture\b0{\*\bkmkstart high-level-architecture}{\*\bkmkend high-level-architecture}\par
\pard\sa80\fs22 The automation pattern uses Configuration Manager to generate bootable OSD media and task sequence content, HPE OneView to identify the target physical host, and HPE iLO to mount the boot ISO and force a one-time boot from virtual media. Once WinPE starts, the server retrieves task sequence policy and content from Configuration Manager and completes the operating system deployment.\par
\pard\sa80\fs22 1. Operator or pipeline identifies the target server by name, serial number, or OneView identifier. 2. Automation queries HPE OneView and validates the target server state. 3. Configuration Manager bootable media ISO is published to a secured repository reachable by iLO virtual media. 4. Automation mounts the ISO through iLO virtual media. 5. Automation sets one-time boot override to virtual CD/DVD and restarts the host. 6. WinPE starts and contacts Configuration Manager management/distribution infrastructure. 7. Task sequence partitions disk, applies operating system, installs drivers and ConfigMgr client, and performs post-install actions. 8. Server reboots to the newly deployed operating system and final validation is completed.\par
\pard\sa120\sb120\fs28\b Prerequisites\b0{\*\bkmkstart prerequisites}{\*\bkmkend prerequisites}\par
\pard\sa120\sb120\fs24\b Technical prerequisites\b0{\*\bkmkstart technical-prerequisites}{\*\bkmkend technical-prerequisites}\par
\pard\li360\fi-360\fs22\'95\tab Configuration Manager console and PowerShell module installed on the administration host.\par\pard\li360\fi-360\fs22\'95\tab Appropriate deployment task sequence created for the target Windows Server version.\par\pard\li360\fi-360\fs22\'95\tab Boot image contains HPE-compatible NIC and storage drivers required in WinPE.\par\pard\li360\fi-360\fs22\'95\tab All required task sequence content distributed to one or more distribution points.\par\pard\li360\fi-360\fs22\'95\tab Target network permits access from WinPE / server to Management Point and Distribution Point as applicable.\par\pard\li360\fi-360\fs22\'95\tab HPE OneView API credentials with rights to query server-hardware objects.\par\pard\li360\fi-360\fs22\'95\tab HPE iLO credentials with rights to perform virtual media and power operations.\par\pard\li360\fi-360\fs22\'95\tab Secure location to host bootable ISO (preferably HTTPS).\par
\pard\sa120\sb120\fs24\b Access prerequisites\b0{\*\bkmkstart access-prerequisites}{\*\bkmkend access-prerequisites}\par
\pard\li360\fi-360\fs22\'95\tab Change approval for production builds (if required by local process).\par\pard\li360\fi-360\fs22\'95\tab Approved service accounts for OneView API and iLO access.\par\pard\li360\fi-360\fs22\'95\tab Access to Configuration Manager site drive / PowerShell context sufficient to create task sequence media.\par\pard\li360\fi-360\fs22\'95\tab Administrative access on the system used to create ConfigMgr media.\par
\pard\sa120\sb120\fs28\b Media Strategy\b0{\*\bkmkstart media-strategy}{\*\bkmkend media-strategy}\par
\pard\sa80\fs22 Preferred approach: use Configuration Manager bootable media (ISO) mounted over iLO virtual media. This is the most flexible option for environments without PXE because the server boots to WinPE from ISO and then retrieves the task sequence and required content from Configuration Manager. Alternative options include stand-alone media for restricted-network scenarios or prestaged media for depot/factory workflows.\par
\pard\li360\fi-360\fs22\'95\tab Preferred: Bootable media ISO - smallest and easiest to maintain; task sequence remains centrally managed.\par\pard\li360\fi-360\fs22\'95\tab Alternative: Stand-alone media - suitable where network access to MP/DP is restricted during build; includes task sequence and content locally.\par\pard\li360\fi-360\fs22\'95\tab Less preferred: Prestaged media - more appropriate for factory / preloaded disk scenarios than for remote iLO-led imaging.\par
\pard\sa120\sb120\fs28\b Standard Operating Procedure\b0{\*\bkmkstart standard-operating-procedure}{\*\bkmkend standard-operating-procedure}\par
\pard\sa120\sb120\fs24\b Prepare or update the Windows Server build in Configuration Manager\b0{\*\bkmkstart prepare-or-update-the-windows-server-build-in-configuration-manager}{\*\bkmkend prepare-or-update-the-windows-server-build-in-configuration-manager}\par
\pard\sa80\fs22 9.Import or update the Windows Server source image within Configuration Manager. 1. Create or update the OSD task sequence for the target operating system build. 2. Add or update HPE driver packages and ensure the required WinPE boot image contains the correct NIC and storage drivers. 3. Distribute all associated content to at least one distribution point. 4. Validate task sequence deployment scope (known / unknown computer support as required).\par
{\pard\sa80\sb80\fs20\fi0\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\clcbpat2{\f1 # Example ConfigMgr media creation command:New-CMBootableMedia -MediaMode Dynamic -MediaType CdDvd -Path "\\\\fileserver\\osdmedia\\WinSrv2025_BootMedia.iso" -AllowUnknownMachine -AllowUnattended -BootImage $BootImage -DistributionPoint $DistributionPoint -ManagementPoint $ManagementPoint -MediaPassword $MediaPassword -Force\f0}\par}
\pard\sa120\sb120\fs24\b Create bootable media ISO\b0{\*\bkmkstart create-bootable-media-iso}{\*\bkmkend create-bootable-media-iso}\par
\pard\sa80\fs22 1. From the Configuration Manager console PowerShell context, create dynamic bootable media as an ISO. 2. Apply a media password where required by policy. 3. Store the ISO in a secured central repository. 4. Version the ISO according to the OSD release standard (for example: WinSrv2025_HPE_BootableMedia_v1.7.iso).\par
\pard\sa120\sb120\fs24\b Publish the ISO for iLO consumption\b0{\*\bkmkstart publish-the-iso-for-ilo-consumption}{\*\bkmkend publish-the-iso-for-ilo-consumption}\par
\pard\sa80\fs22 1. Place the ISO in a location accessible to iLO virtual media. 2. Prefer HTTPS with controlled access and auditable hosting. 3. Validate the full ISO path / URL before initiating the build.\par
\pard\sa80\fs22 10.4 Identify and validate the target server in HPE OneView\par
\pard\sa80\fs22 1. Query HPE OneView for the target physical server by name, serial number, Bay/Enclosure position, or other approved identifier. 2. Verify the hardware state, power state, and health state before proceeding. 3. Confirm the correct server has been selected and is approved for build / rebuild. 4. Resolve or derive the corresponding iLO management address or endpoint for the server.\par
{\pard\sa80\sb80\fs20\fi0\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\clcbpat2{\f1 # Example OneView REST query pattern:GET https://<oneview-appliance>/rest/server-hardware?filter="name='<ServerName>'"\f0}\par}
\pard\sa120\sb120\fs24\b Mount ISO via HPE iLO and force one-time boot\b0{\*\bkmkstart mount-iso-via-hpe-ilo-and-force-one-time-boot}{\*\bkmkend mount-iso-via-hpe-ilo-and-force-one-time-boot}\par
\pard\sa80\fs22 1. Authenticate to the target iLO using a service account with virtual media and power control rights. 2. Insert the ConfigMgr bootable ISO as virtual media. 3. Set a one-time boot override to the virtual CD/DVD device. 4. Restart or power on the physical server. 5. Observe console output or iLO event logs to verify the host boots to WinPE.\par
{\pard\sa80\sb80\fs20\fi0\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\clcbpat2{\f1 # Example Redfish operations (conceptual):POST /redfish/v1/Managers/1/VirtualMedia/<DeviceId>/Actions/VirtualMedia.InsertMediaPATCH /redfish/v1/Systems/1 \{ BootSourceOverrideEnabled: "Once", BootSourceOverrideTarget: "Cd" \}POST /redfish/v1/Systems/1/Actions/ComputerSystem.Reset\f0}\par}
\pard\sa120\sb120\fs24\b Task sequence execution\b0{\*\bkmkstart task-sequence-execution}{\*\bkmkend task-sequence-execution}\par
\pard\sa80\fs22 1. WinPE starts from the bootable ISO. 2. he server connects to the Configuration Manager Management Point and downloads task sequence policy. 3. Disk partitioning and formatting are performed according to task sequence standards. 4. The operating system image is applied. 5. Drivers and the Configuration Manager client are installed. 6. Post-install steps execute, such as domain join, security baseline, management agent installation, and standard software configuration. 7. The system reboots into the installed operating system. 8. Post-build validation is completed and the build record is updated.\par
\pard\sa120\sb120\fs28\b Validation Checklist\b0{\*\bkmkstart validation-checklist}{\*\bkmkend validation-checklist}\par
\pard\sa120\sb120\fs24\b Pre-build validation\b0{\*\bkmkstart pre-build-validation}{\*\bkmkend pre-build-validation}\par
\pard\li360\fi-360\fs22\'95\tab Correct target server identified in OneView.\par\pard\li360\fi-360\fs22\'95\tab Target approved for imaging / rebuild.\par\pard\li360\fi-360\fs22\'95\tab Task sequence and required content available in Configuration Manager.\par\pard\li360\fi-360\fs22\'95\tab Boot image includes required HPE WinPE drivers.\par\pard\li360\fi-360\fs22\'95\tab ISO path validated and reachable.\par\pard\li360\fi-360\fs22\'95\tab Network path to MP/DP validated for the target VLAN or build network.\par\pard\li360\fi-360\fs22\'95\tab iLO credentials verified.\par\pard\li360\fi-360\fs22\'95\tab Configuration / change record created where required.\par
\pard\sa120\sb120\fs24\b In-build validation\b0{\*\bkmkstart in-build-validation}{\*\bkmkend in-build-validation}\par
\pard\li360\fi-360\fs22\'95\tab ISO mounted successfully in iLO virtual media.\par\pard\li360\fi-360\fs22\'95\tab One-time boot override applied.\par\pard\li360\fi-360\fs22\'95\tab System boots to WinPE.\par\pard\li360\fi-360\fs22\'95\tab Task sequence is visible / starts correctly.\par\pard\li360\fi-360\fs22\'95\tab Disk operations complete successfully.\par\pard\li360\fi-360\fs22\'95\tab OS image apply completes successfully.\par\pard\li360\fi-360\fs22\'95\tab Task sequence reaches final restart with no blocking errors.\par
\pard\sa120\sb120\fs24\b Post-build validation\b0{\*\bkmkstart post-build-validation}{\*\bkmkend post-build-validation}\par
\pard\li360\fi-360\fs22\'95\tab Expected hostname assigned.\par\pard\li360\fi-360\fs22\'95\tab Domain join successful (if required).\par\pard\li360\fi-360\fs22\'95\tab Correct OU placement or directory registration.\par\pard\li360\fi-360\fs22\'95\tab Operating system version, edition, and patch baseline verified.\par\pard\li360\fi-360\fs22\'95\tab Expected HPE device drivers present.\par\pard\li360\fi-360\fs22\'95\tab Configuration Manager client healthy and assigned to site.\par\pard\li360\fi-360\fs22\'95\tab RDP / PowerShell / management agents operational.\par\pard\li360\fi-360\fs22\'95\tab Build outcome captured in operational records.\par
\pard\sa120\sb120\fs28\b Rollback / Recovery Procedure\b0{\*\bkmkstart rollback-recovery-procedure}{\*\bkmkend rollback-recovery-procedure}\par
\pard\sa80\fs22 1. If the task sequence fails before OS application, eject virtual media, reset boot order to normal, and investigate WinPE / network / driver issues. 2. If the task sequence fails after partial deployment, either rerun the build after remediation or wipe/reinitialize the local storage before retry. 3. If the wrong server was selected, stop the workflow immediately, eject media, cancel the change, and follow incident / change procedures. 4. If iLO virtual media operations fail, validate device index, iLO generation, ISO accessibility, and Redfish permission scope.\par
\pard\sa120\sb120\fs28\b Troubleshooting Guide\b0{\*\bkmkstart troubleshooting-guide}{\*\bkmkend troubleshooting-guide}\par
